  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">GIZ Grant Agreement</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Democratic Republic of the Congo):  Leveraging the German Cooperation&apos;s proven expertise in improving water service delivery, USAID will expand drinking water and basic sanitation access by improving local governance of the water sector. USAID will support the development of a strong and credible regulatory framework that clearly separates the policymaking (executive), regulatory, and service delivery functions within the water sector and strengthens the Provincial Water Services Authority in North Kivu, South Kivu, Kasai Oriental, and Lomami...With FY 2022 funds, USAID will work with the central-level Ministry of Hydraulic Resources and Electricity to establish and operationalize the national regulatory authority for the water sector, ensure compliance with applicable laws, standards, and contracts, establish a system for the arbitration of disputes, and monitor water prices. At the provincial level, FY 2022 funds will support setting, measuring, and enforcing standards of the Provincial Water Services Authority, build its capacity to fulfill its role as project owner, support an efficient operator organization for service management, and engage communities to increase their ownership and mitigate conflict...This activity will contribute to Mission Objective 2.2 (Expand U.S. investment and economic ties by supporting anti-corruption efforts, enhancing security, promoting transparent governance systems, establishing a more cost-effective regulatory framework, and enabling a more investor-friendly business environment) by supporting policy interventions and regulatory frameworks that facilitate private sector participation in water service delivery. Increased private sector engagement maximizes taxpayer investments and advances Administrator Power&apos;s Localization Agenda. Furthermore, this activity supports the U.S. Global Water Strategy, which defines water security as a national security priority...</narrative>
  </description>
